1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Etnesoga I page 407, Etnesoga II page 362 Norheim (1). (Men begge steder er det feil, f.eks. var det nok denne Lisbet Nilsdtr. Bugge som var g.m. Tolleiv Bjørnson Norheim, og ikke søsteren Birgitte Nilsdtr. Bugge s
2 CONC om var ugift i 1606).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisbet var ikke mor til alle barna som er oppført i Etnesoga II side 362 og 363. Salg av arvegods etter Bjørn Tolleivson Helgeland på Steinsland i Sandeid i april 1698, som var barnløs, viser at Tolleiv Bjørnson Norheim hadde 5 ba
2 CONC rn med første kona Lisbet, og 7 barn med andre kona. Barna med Lisbet var i aldersrekkefølge Sakarias på Norheim, Lisbet/Elisabet på Hauge i Hjelmeland, Madela på Frette, Anna på Hauge i Ølen og Høyland i Etne, og yngst Anna på Ve
2 CONC  i Etne. Jeg kjenner ingen henvising til primærkilder som oppgir fornavnet til den prestedattera Nielsdtr. Bugge som Tolleiv Bjørnson Norheim først var gift med. Men da alle de 5 barna hadde døtre med navn Lisbet, er det vel nå an
2 CONC tatt at fornavnet var Lisbet. Eldste dattera til Tolleiv Bjørnson Norheim i hans andre ekteskap hadde navnet Lisbet, og hun var nok da som ikke var uvanlig blitt oppkalt etter faren Tolleiv sin første kone. Navnet Lisbet oppgir og
2 CONC så Yngve Nedrebø ved statsarkivet i Bergen som mest sannsynlig. Fornavnet Birgitte som tidligere ofte er oppgitt var vel hennes søster som trolig var ugift i 1606, se nedenfor (Oppgitt av Helge Bjørgen).
2 CONT
2 CONT Et gavebrev til latinskolen i 1606 fra Niels Bugge er underskrevet av hans sønn Hans Nielsson Bugge, svoger Tolleif Bjørnson Norheim og Niels Bugge sin datter Birgitte Nielsdtr. Siden Birgitte selv skrev unnder, var hun nok da ikk
2 CONC e gift. Derfor var det nok Birgitte sin søster Lisbet Nielsdtr. Bugge som var gift med Tolleif Bjørnson Norheim. I odelsmanntallet fra 1624 heter det at sønnen Hans Nielsson Bugge arvet halvparten av faren sitt pantegods. Den andr
2 CONC e halvparten må da ha tilfalt de to døtrene Lisbet og Birgitte, og Niels Pedersen Bugge har nok ikke hatt barna Christen, Mette, Thomas og Sara som eldre slektstavler oppgir. Lisbet Nielsdtr. Bugge må være død før 1611 (eller skal
2 CONC  det være død før 1621?), for da ble eldste sønnen til Tolleiv i andre ekteskap født. Se Rotvoll-slekta av Per Ivar Rotvoll Tautra utgitt 2000, side 117-120.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16284. Tolleiv* BJØRNSSON Norheim(706) (706)(751) (705) was born about 1565 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. He died in 1637 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. Tolleiv took over Norheim from his father in 1
2 CONC 603 and operated the farm for the rest of his life. He was an extremely rich landowner and must have been in the upper social strata of Etne since he married the priest's daughter. Tolleiv inherited extensive properties and increa
2 CONC sed the size of his estate by purchasing additional land. In 1615, he was one of the largest allodial landowners in Etne and was required to support a soldier. Tolleiv served as a lagrettemann and represented Etne at the Royal Cor
2 CONC onation in Oslo in 1610. He was also one of the men who witnessed Nils Pedersson Bugge's gift of 200 riksdalar to the Bergen Cathedral school in 1606. In fact, Tolleiv signed his own name on the document, indicating he could proba
2 CONC bly read and write. In 1624, Tolleiv owned property at Norheim, Ekrheim, Østbø, Bleie, Sekse, Aldensøe (probably Askvol in Sogn) and Brecke. The total value of his estate was about 7 laupar smør and 3 laupar salt. He probably acqu
2 CONC ired additional property later since his wife's brother was in possession of over 13 laupar smør owned by their deceased father that had not yet been divided among the heirs. He was married to Birgitte* NIELSDATTER Bugge about 159
2 CONC 5 in Etne, Hordaland, Norway.(706) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16285. Birgitte* NIELSDATTER Bugge(706) (706)(751) (705) was born about 1580 in Etne, Hordaland, Norway. She died in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. Birgitte witnessed her father's gift of 200 riksdalar to the Bergen Ca
2 CONC thedral school on 13 Aug 1606. Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8142 i. Sakarias* TOLLEIVSSON Norheim. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii. Anna TOLLEIVSDATTER Norheim(706) (705) was born about 1605 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. She died about 1675 in Ve farm #20, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii. Anna TOLLEIVSDATTER Norheim(706) (705) was born about 1605 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. She died before 1655 in Høyland farm #48, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  iv. Jon TOLLEIVSSON Skjold(706) (751)(705) was born about 1615 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. He died in 1666 in Skjold farm #61, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. Jon Tolleivsson appears to have been a relatively wealthy m
2 CONC an. He didn't move to Skjold until sometime in the 1660's, shortly before his death. Jon probably lived at one of the farms owned by the Norheim family and allowed his father-in-law to operate Skjold. Skjold was a farm of 1 laup 6
2 CONC  merker smør. It supported a herd of 1 horse, 12 cattle and 18 sheep and goats. In 1666, Jon owned property at Norheim, Ekrheim, Håland and Rame, besides Skjold where he was living at the time of his death. He was last named in Ja
2 CONC n 1667 when he paid his brother 11 riksdalar to settle an old inheritance issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  v. Johannes TOLLEIVSSON Erøy(706) (712)(705) was born in 1626 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. He died in Erøy farm, Erfjord, Rogaland, Norway. Johannes Tolleivsson is mentioned in the 1661 and 1666 tax lists as the 
2 CONC farmer of 3 laupar smør at Erøy. He probably came to Erøy around 1654 after his father-in-law, who owned the farm, moved to Imsland. Johannes is also mentioned in a document of 1667 in which his brother paid him 11 dalar because h
2 CONC e had received too little of the inheritance after their father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  vi. Lisbet TOLLEIVSDATTER Norheim(706) (715)(705) was born about 1600 in Norheim farm #49, Etne, Hordaland, Norway. She died after 1645 in Ekrheim farm #71, Etne, Hordaland, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
